Z||000000||normalicy||05-11-2001||05:03 AM||||The info:<BR>Just swapped an 2.5L from an '84 manual transmission fiero to a '85 with an automatic.<P>Problems:<BR>First, I had to swap flywheels in order to mount the torq converter.  However, the '84 engine's crank sticks out about 1/4" (because the manual flywheel was about that thick).  So, I couldn't tighten the bolts down with an impact... or any socketed wrench since there was no space between the bolt and the protrusion.<P>Second, I believe that the first problem is causing my starter to whirr for a second or two after starting the car.<P>Third, when the car gets above the 55mph mark, it feels as if it is stuck in second (sorta stressing, never feels like it levels off) despite my checking to be sure that it is shifting into all 3 gears while driving slowly.  My guesses are that the torq converter isn't engaging all the way or that something else that I haven't thought of (exhaust?).<P>Thanks everyone.<P>------------------<BR>What is normal anyway?||||reg||1
